# game: this repository
#
# name is the project: it is the block in the builder's own config that
# says where this tree's two remotes are. nothing here holds a remote,
# and a builder who has no block for it builds locally.
name kingfisher-dist

# the contact the imagery and weather providers ask every client to
# declare. it is the operator's name and address, so it is set in their
# own config and never written here.
needs KINGFISHER_CONTACT a name and address the data providers can reach

# the lint kingfisher holds. a repository that describes any lint describes
# all of it, so this list is the whole of it, and the card is not on it:
# kingfisher is the largest thing here, its readme is a manpage rather than
# a screen, and its reference pages are long because the surface is.
lint width 80
lint comments
lint exclaim
lint shout
lint paragraph 4
lint words hyperscaler enterprise-grade blazing-fast load-bearing

# the two reference pages are let off two rules. a page of conditions and
# a page of instructions run to more than four lines at a time, and both
# name headers, environment variables and verbs in capitals because that
# is what those things are called. every other page here is held to both.
lint allow USING.md paragraph shout
lint allow OPERATION.md paragraph shout

# the readme is a manpage rather than a screen: fifty-nine lines, a third
# of them bird. in a stack the strictest rule wins, so the card is waived
# for this one page by name rather than by the dotfile's absence.
lint allow README.md rows

# the suite, as a target, so a stack build runs it the way a person does:
# uv brings pytest, the repository brings the rest.
target test . :: uv run --with pytest python -m pytest -q --no-header -p no:cacheprovider tests
